&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"&gt;USGPC's asset retirement obligations include reclamation requirements as regulated by government authorities related to USGPC's natural gas pipeline. The accounting for asset retirement obligations requires estimates by management about the timing of asset retirements, the cost of retirement obligations, discount and inflation rates used in determining fair values and the methods of remediation associated with its asset retirement obligations. USGPC uses assumptions and estimates that reflect the most likely remediation method. USGPC's estimated liability for asset retirement obligations is revised whenever events or changes in circumstances indicate that a revision to the estimate is necessary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Operating Expenses&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"&gt;USGPC has no dedicated personnel of its own and is operated by personnel of its affiliate, USGypsum, and its parent, USG Corporation. Operating expenses consist primarily of personnel and overhead costs from those entities and costs for outside professional services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"&gt;USGPC transports natural gas for shippers under a tariff regulated by the FERC. The tariff specifies the general terms and conditions of transportation service on the natural gas pipeline system. Our revenues are derived from agreements for the receipt and delivery of natural gas at points along the pipeline system as specified in each shipper's individual transportation contract. USGPC does not own the natural gas that it transports.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"&gt;Revenue is recognized in the month in which the contractual performance obligations are satisfied, which is during the month in which the transportation services are provided. USGPC's contracts are on an interruptible basis and USGPC does not have an obligation to perform the transportation service until the customer's request has been accepted. Revenue for these transportation services is fee-based, valued based on the rate in effect for the month of service per quantity that the customer choses to and that USGPC accepted. Revenue is recognized in the month of service based on the volumes of natural gas USGPC transports. Payment is generally received from the customer in the month following performance of the services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&amp;#xa0;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"&gt;Subsequent events were evaluated for potential recognition or disclosure through April 6, 2025, which is the date the financial statements were available to be issued.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note 3 &lt;/b&gt;-&lt;b&gt; Associated Company Transactions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

